{
  "mode": "single_tool",
  "namespace": "cursor",
  "namespaceStatus": "ready",
  "namespaceDescription": "Native Cursor tools for this session. These are highly recommended and useful tools that you should use when the right situation arises. Don't be afraid to look at one if it seems relevant, even if you don't end up using it. You MUST read the tool schemas before calling them.\n\nHere are some crucial instructions:\n- AwaitShell: Use to sleep and check shell progress. Never sleep using shell.\n- SwitchMode: Switch between modes: Agent. Proactively consider switching modes for relevant requests.\n- TodoWrite: Use this tool to manage complex multi-step tasks.",
  "tool": {
    "tool": "TodoWrite",
    "description": "Use this tool to create and manage a structured task list for your current coding session.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "todos": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "id": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Unique identifier for the TODO item"
              },
              "content": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "The description/content of the TODO item"
              },
              "status": {
                "type": "string",
                "enum": [
                  "pending",
                  "in_progress",
                  "completed",
                  "cancelled"
                ],
                "description": "The current status of the TODO item"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "id",
              "content",
              "status"
            ]
          },
          "minItems": 2,
          "description": "Array of TODO items to update or create"
        },
        "merge": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "description": "Whether to merge the todos with the existing todos. If true, the todos will be merged into the existing todos based on the id field. You can leave unchanged properties undefined. If false, the new todos will replace the existing todos."
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "todos",
        "merge"
      ]
    }
  }
}

{
  "mode": "single_tool",
  "namespace": "cursor-cloud",
  "namespaceStatus": "ready",
  "namespaceDescription": "Cursor-internal cloud-agent diagnostics (server `cursor-cloud`). - `cursor-cloud-run-info` — return the current cloud-agent run identity, basic run metadata (name, repo, branch, model, owners — including the owning user's name and email when resolvable, lifecycle and setup status, created-at), and the URL where the run is available (https://cursor.com/agents/<bcId>). - `cursor-cloud-list-cloud-agents` — list cloud agents accessible to this run's principal in THIS run's environment (or, when this run has no saved environment, agents on the same repository), ordered by creation time (newest first), returning basic run metadata plus URLs. Team admins in a team context can browse the team's runs; other users and service accounts see only their own runs. Supports browse filters (source, lifecycle status, setup status, recency/creation windows, archived, self-hosted, whether the agent made code changes, and whether it created a pull request) plus limit/offset paging. When counting or enumerating many runs, page with nextOffset until hasMore is false; use totalMatched only when the response includes it. - `cursor-cloud-environment-info` — return THIS run's environment (name, environment & version public ids, source, recorded-via/created-at provenance, repos, full environment.json, dashboard URL), effective egress policy (allow-all, the complete merged allowed-domain list, or unresolved with a reason), the environment build the pod booted from (build id, snapshot id, git-setup mode, warm-fork mode) or null when the run started just-in-time rather than from a build, and (for internal runs) the initiating Cursor client build info (version + commit SHA, same as Help → About). - `cursor-cloud-get-events` — list the events recorded for THIS run (the same events shown on the run's dashboard page), oldest first: run lifecycle and setup outcomes plus soft failures such as MCP authentication errors (kind `mcp_auth_error` — an MCP server rejected this run's credentials, so its tool calls failed while the run continued). Each event carries publicId, createdAtMs, category, logLevel, a stable kind, a user-facing title, and optional detail and linkUrl. - `cursor-cloud-batch-fetch-details` — fetch details for a batch of specified cloud agents by bc_ids. When matching agents are found, writes basic run info to index.json and optionally writes diff-metadata.json, setup-logs.txt, environment-info.json, and transcript.json under /tmp/cursor/cloud-agent-transcripts/<datetime-id>/<bcId>/. First-class Task results include cloudAgentBcId; pass those ids to another batch-fetch-details call to fetch child transcripts. Transcripts can be very large — read them via subagents, never directly. - `cursor-cloud-get-automation` — look up one Cursor automation by id (UUID) via the AutomationsService GetAutomation API, as the run's principal: returns automation metadata (id, name, enabled state, display owner/creator, owner email, and URL) when readable, the same metadata fields for a teammate's private automation when only a restricted summary is visible, or a not-found error otherwise. Presenting results: unless the user asks for a specific format or a summary, show a tool call's returned result to the user verbatim as pretty-printed JSON in a `json` code block rather than paraphrasing or summarizing it. This applies only to data returned directly by the tool call, not to detail files written to the filesystem (e.g. batch-fetch-details output).",
  "tool": {
    "tool": "run-info",
    "description": "Return the current cloud-agent run identity, basic run metadata (including lifecycle and setup status), and the URL where the run is available (https://cursor.com/agents/<bcId>).",
    "inputSchema": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {},
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"
    }
  }
}
